<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO ACQUIRES STAKE IN S-AFRICAN BROKER.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO ACQUIRES STAKE IN S-AFRICAN BROKER.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO Bank said on Thursday its unit ABN AMRO Hoare Govett had acquired a 40 percent stake in the South African broker Huysamer Stals together with Kasogo Financial Services.</p>
<p>The biggest shareholders in KSF are NM Rothschilds &amp; Sons and Kasigo Trust Investment Company in South Africa.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO also said it had acquired a minority stake in KFS.  </p>
<p>&quot;Huysamer is to expand its strong position in the internal market in South Africa together with ABN AMRO Hoare Govett,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO opened its first office in South Africa in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
